---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Crumbs from '../components/Crumbs.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
import { crumbLd, webPageLd } from '../lib/ld';

const crumbs = [{ name: 'Terms', path: '/terms/' }];
const desc = 'Terms of use for WeldFacts.com. Specs are transcriptions of manufacturer pages. The manufacturer manual governs the machine.';
const jsonld = [webPageLd('Terms of use', '/terms/', desc, SITE.checked), crumbLd(crumbs)];
---
<Base title="Terms of use" description={desc} path="/terms/" og="/og/page-terms.png" jsonld={jsonld}>
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <div class="pagehead">
      <Crumbs crumbs={crumbs} />
      <h1>Terms of use</h1>
    </div>
    <p>These terms cover use of WeldFacts.com. The pages are transcriptions of manufacturer specifications as of the read date on the <a href="/how-we-verify/">source rules</a> page. Manufacturers change products, manuals, and spec sheets. The manual and the labeling that ship with a machine govern that machine. If a cell on this site and the manual in your hand disagree, follow the manual and send the URL of the newer source to {SITE.email}.</p>
    <h2>The job check</h2>
    <p>The job check compares numbers you type with numbers the manufacturer published. It is not an electrical inspection, not a permit, and not a statement that a circuit is safe. A pass does not prove the breaker in the wall is the size you typed. A fail does not describe how to modify a panel. Welding and branch-circuit work can injure people and start fires. This site does not provide instructions for either.</p>
    <h2>Names and independence</h2>
    <p>Product names identify machines so the cited sheet can be found. The names belong to their owners. WeldFacts is not those companies and not Amazon. Nothing on the site is a joint offer with a manufacturer.</p>
    <h2>Links and money</h2>
    <p>Amazon links use the Associates tag weldfacts-20. WeldFacts may earn a fee if you buy through them. The fee does not change a spec. No price is published here. The <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a> describes search links and direct links. Other outbound links go to manufacturer PDFs and product pages. Those sites have their own terms.</p>
    <h2>Use of the pages</h2>
    <p>You may read the pages and quote a spec if you keep the meaning and the fact that it came from the manufacturer source linked on the row. You may not present the tables as your own measurements or strip the "not published" mark off a blank cell. Automated collection of the public pages is allowed. The <a href="/llms.txt">llms.txt</a> file points at the same material. Do not invent a spec that a row marks unpublished and attribute it to this site.</p>
    <p>The pages are provided as a reference, without a warranty that every future manual revision is already reflected. Liability for how you use a machine or a circuit stays with the person doing the work. Questions about these terms go to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
